# Titan Orbit — Windows late-join crash invariants (HARD STOP)

> **Agents:** start with the short always-on rule `titan-orbit-teamchoice-crash-hardstop.mdc`.
> Use `ClientJoinSettleCache.ShouldSkipShipEntityQueries` / `ShouldSkipMapBodyQueries` — never invent Settling-only gates.

**Status (proven 2026-07-18 / updated 2026-07-22):** Relay late-join survives when `TransformQuarantine` gates map-body gathers, GhostSpawn stays CreateEntity-all + Instantiates 1/frame, hybrid map GOs queue via Instantiates hook (not asteroid scans), and ship presentation skips `GhostSpawnBacklog` after Join Team. Agents keep undoing this. Treat any “cleanup” that removes these gates as a **regression bug**, not a refactor.

Paired: `titan-orbit-ship-simulation.mdc`, embedded NetCode (`Packages/com.unity.netcode`), `tools/netcode-patches/`.

If your task touches **any** file in the ownership list below, read this whole rule first and keep every invariant.

---

## What actually crashes (not “CPU overload”)

`Crash!!!` in Player.log is a **native access violation** in Burst / UnityPlayer (often `GatherEntitiesWithoutFilter`, LocalToWorld jobs, or GhostReceive). C# `try/catch` **cannot** catch it. Soft rate-limits and nicer loading UI do **not** fix it.

Two progress bars do **not** prevent the crash. They only show phases. Gates + Instantiates caps + real GO proxies prevent death.

**Editor ≠ Windows client.** Local host / Editor Play Mode can load the map fine while the Windows player dies. Always treat Windows Relay late-join Player.log as the source of truth for join safety.

